.TITLE "copy"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Copies one or more files to another location. It creates a duplicate of the source file at the destination path.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**copy source destination**
Copies a file from the source path to the destination path.
> __source__ the file to copy | __destination__ the target location

**copy *.txt destination**
Copies all text files in the current directory to the destination.
> __*.txt__ wildcard for text files

**copy /v source destination**
Verifies that the new files are written correctly.
> __/v__ verify flag

**copy /y source destination**
Suppresses prompting to confirm you want to overwrite an existing destination file.
> __/y__ overwrite flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __/y__ flag is essential for automation in scripts to avoid pausing for user input. For copying entire directory trees, consider using **windows:robocopy** instead.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:move** **windows:del**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/copy__
